{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02742",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.32,
      "end_seconds": 5.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "hello? Doctor? I was told to come in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.0,
      "end_seconds": 9.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.62,
      "end_seconds": 24.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.43,
      "text": "well I've been having a widespread rash with fever. I did try to ignore it for a while. My family kept telling me to get it checked"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.43,
      "end_seconds": 27.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.34,
      "end_seconds": 31.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "it it happens on and off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.49,
      "end_seconds": 35.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.38,
      "end_seconds": 51.81,
      "duration_seconds": 15.43,
      "text": "when it starts I tend to get swollen face as well the swollen face? That's been for about two weeks as for swollen face maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.35,
      "end_seconds": 61.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "I see go ahead. Have you had a widespread rash with fever before or is this the the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.5,
      "end_seconds": 70.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Mm, yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.94,
      "end_seconds": 77.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.98,
      "end_seconds": 85.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Yes anxiety. Arthritis in my knees for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.27,
      "end_seconds": 95.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "alright, anxiety, that matches what I have here right, which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.45,
      "end_seconds": 105.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "It's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety. Diclofenac. I take it when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.83,
      "end_seconds": 113.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.74,
      "end_seconds": 118.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "50 milligrams. Allopurinol. I take it started four weeks ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.88,
      "end_seconds": 121.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.67,
      "end_seconds": 123.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "300 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.93,
      "end_seconds": 126.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.5,
      "end_seconds": 131.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "About a month now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.89,
      "end_seconds": 137.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "right, any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.81,
      "end_seconds": 145.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "my grandfather had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.76,
      "end_seconds": 164.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.29,
      "end_seconds": 168.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.76,
      "end_seconds": 173.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Alright do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.49,
      "end_seconds": 177.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I swim twice a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.96,
      "end_seconds": 183.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.34,
      "end_seconds": 187.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "yes, I'm allergic to naproxen"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.39,
      "end_seconds": 193.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "a few quick ones: breathing difficulty, blisters or mouth sores?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.47,
      "end_seconds": 199.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "no, no breathing difficulty, blisters or mouth sores"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.41,
      "end_seconds": 203.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.28,
      "end_seconds": 207.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "no that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.01,
      "end_seconds": 211.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.82,
      "end_seconds": 223.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.29,
      "end_seconds": 243.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 107 over 75, pulse is 107 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 95 percent, temp 38.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.16,
      "end_seconds": 246.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.49,
      "end_seconds": 254.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "So, they help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.78,
      "end_seconds": 262.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.97,
      "end_seconds": 272.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.49,
      "end_seconds": 276.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "tell me if that's sore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.47,
      "end_seconds": 291.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "There is a widespread red rash facial swelling and your temperature is high with enlarged glands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.49,
      "end_seconds": 294.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.27,
      "end_seconds": 302.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "That's all I needed to to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.02,
      "end_seconds": 346.54,
      "duration_seconds": 34.52,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be a severe drug reaction, or it might be a viral rash. Urgent blood tests is what I'd like next, for severe drug reaction. I'm prescribing prednisolone, 40 milligrams, once a day, until review. That should help with severe drug reaction. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.36,
      "end_seconds": 374.45,
      "duration_seconds": 27.09,
      "text": "Stop the allopurinol now and you need admission. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Please come and see me straight away. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.22,
      "end_seconds": 376.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "that's clear, thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.51,
      "end_seconds": 379.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Okay, take care now."
    }
  ]
}